ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: yellow
REAL_USE_CASE: Vector DB users (Chroma, Milvus, LangChain, LlamaIndex) who select SentenceTransformer models with shipped prompts (e.g., arctic-embed family) for RAG/semantic search; the wrapper's default encode() path silently drops the prompt, losing 9-63pp R@10 in production.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Real win, not microbench-only. In-situ Chroma 1.5.9 reproduces the loss: default R@10=0.7226 vs encode_query()=0.8229 on SciFact (-9.4pp, plus HNSW approx). Effect generalizes across 3 models (arctic-embed-s +9.4pp, -m +63.2pp, -xs +14.8pp) and 2 datasets (SciFact +9.4pp, NFCorpus +2.9pp). The seam is at the wrapper boundary, not inside ST.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Wrapper defaults must change: Chroma ST subclass does not override embed_query; pymilvus query_instruction=""; LangChain query_encode_kwargs={}; LlamaIndex query_instruction=None. Users must manually discover and specify prompts, or maintainers must fix defaults to honor model.config prompts via encode_query(). The model self-describes (prompts in config, default_prompt_name=null) but ST.encode() applies nothing, creating silent failure for competent users.]
RATIONALE: The decisive test confirms the seam is real (A=0.7292 vs B=0.8229, AB_embeddings_identical=False; packet lines 12-15). In-situ Chroma lands on A-number (0.7226), losing the +9.4pp (packet lines 17-20). Cross-model and cross-dataset generalization confirmed (packet lines 22-27). However, the mechanism "prompts help" is decades-known (E5/Wang2022, Instructor/TART cited in packet). The contribution is the integration-default seam and its silent invisibility, not a new mechanism. This is a solid, reproducible packaging/integration finding with measurable production impact, but modest in altitude—an honest YELLOW, not a GREEN. The negative result is actionable: wrapper maintainers must honor model prompts by default.
```
